# Build context for the apps/api production image.
#
# Two jobs: keep the context small (it is uploaded to the daemon on every build)
# and keep host artefacts out of the image. Everything the api build needs is
# listed as an explicit COPY in the Dockerfile, so anything excluded here that
# turns out to be required fails loudly at build time rather than silently.
#
# NOTE ON THE `dir/*` + `!dir/file` PATTERN BELOW: the exclusion is written
# against the directory's *children* (`apps/web/*`), never the directory itself
# (`apps/web`). Docker evaluates re-inclusions reliably that way; excluding the
# directory node itself and then trying to re-include a file inside it is the
# formulation that behaves differently across builder implementations.

# --- Never, under any circumstances ---
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/.next
**/out

# Secrets and local environment.
#
# The `**/` prefix is load-bearing. Bare `.env` / `.env.*` match ONLY the
# context root, so `apps/api/.env` — which is exactly where this repo tells
# developers to put OPENAI_API_KEY, JWT_SECRET and the R2 credentials
# (apps/api/.env.example) — sailed straight into the build stage via
# `COPY apps/api apps/api`. Verified by building the `build` target and listing
# the file inside it.
#
# It never reached the runtime image, but the deploy workflow uses
# `cache-to: type=gha,mode=max`, which exports every intermediate layer to the
# GitHub Actions cache. So the blast radius was real.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.envrc
**/.direnv
!**/.env.example

# VCS and tooling metadata
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Docker/deploy artefacts — none of these belong inside the image, and touching
# them must not bust the build cache.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
Caddyfile
postgres.conf
scripts

# Documentation and repo prose
**/*.md
docs
CONTEXT.md

# --- Workspaces that are not part of this image ---
# Their package.json files are kept: `npm ci` validates the lockfile against the
# full workspace graph and refuses to install if one is missing, even though the
# install itself is filtered to api + @repo/schemas.
apps/web/*
!apps/web/package.json
apps/mcp/*
!apps/mcp/package.json
apps/extractor/*
!apps/extractor/package.json
apps/training/*
!apps/training/package.json
packages/ui/*
!packages/ui/package.json
packages/eslint-config/*
!packages/eslint-config/package.json

# --- api sources that are not needed to build or run ---
apps/api/**/*.test.ts
apps/api/vitest.config.ts
apps/api/src/test-setup.ts
apps/api/src/infra/http/test-support
